<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resource-shrinker keep rules (§6.8).

  isShrinkResources removes any resource it cannot see referenced. It reads
  R.<type>.<name> references in code and @type/name in XML — and nothing else.
  Both of the resource families below are reached only by name at runtime:

      CompanyLogo.kt   getIdentifier("logo_$key", "drawable", packageName)
      FieldLabels.kt   getIdentifier("tpl_${templateId}_$fieldKey", "string", ...)

  A composed string is invisible to that analysis, so the shrinker concluded the
  whole set was dead and deleted it. The release build kept 0 of 593 logo
  drawables and 12 of 119 template label strings, which is why every institution
  fell back to a monogram and most field labels fell back to a humanised field
  id — in the Play build only. Debug never shrinks, so it all looked correct
  right up until the artifact that reaches users.

  This is the same failure mode as the Room R8 crash: the tooling is silent, the
  build is green, and only the shipped artifact is wrong. Prefer R.string /
  R.drawable references where possible; when a lookup must be dynamic, its
  resources have to be named here or they will not ship.
-->
<resources
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/logo_*,@string/tpl_*" />
